{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804271-principle-renegades","id":804271,"title":"Principle Renegades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-08T23:17:48-08:00","id":804271,"title":"Principle Renegades","content":"Just a crossover-style thought experiment I was toying around with: as I understand it, <i>qashmallim</i> can't Fall; but let's say they could, and let's further stipulate that the result bears a resemblance to the Unchained in the same way that the Principle bears a resemblance to the GM and how <i>qashmallim</i> resemble the GM's Angels. How would they <i>differ</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:20:13-08:00","id":804353,"title":"","content":"Considering their source, I'd say they would have <i>some</i> interaction with Pyros, Azoth, and Flux, thus with Disquiet and Wasteland.<br /> <br /> Exactly <i>what</i>, though...<br /> <hr /><br /> Well, I doubt Fallen Quashmal need to worry overmuch about the Principle hunting them down. From a games/meta standpoint, that means they need some other limiter. Probably the Disquiet/Wasteland rules. Maybe they don't need to hide, so much as keep their powers restrained for fear of breaking stuff.<br /> <hr /><br /> 2 Wild Mass Guesses on how they may <i>already</i> exist:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>GM Angels <i>are</i> &quot;Fallen&quot; Quashmallim. Part of the Occult Matrix that &quot;summons&quot; a new Angel is the G-M determining when a Quashmal will manifest. The other part being the G-M's own Angel Jacking - Hooking the Q's mind up to the Machine's data feeds, brainwashing them, reconfiguration to use the Essence supplied by Infrastructure instead of Pyros, and custom equipment/modifications to fulfill their designated purpose. It kind fits thematically, too: The Principle, and thus Quashmallim, care about choice - something the G-M, and thus its Angels, care not at all about (if not outright reject). This makes the <u>choice</u> of a Demon's Fall either the Principle in action, or an inherent bug in the design.</li> <li>&quot;Fallen&quot; Quashmal are where the Divine Fire that animates a Promethean comes from (or maybe just the Progenitors?). An extra-temporal Quashmal chooses to assist a desperate demiurge in their goals, and inhabits the body, becoming the Promethean. It's Pyros is the Promethean's Pyros. The Pilgrimage becomes their Purpose. Other Quashmal are helping/teaching their fallen peers.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:06:35-08:00","id":804685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804271-principle-renegades?p=804353#post804353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GM Angels <i>are</i> &quot;Fallen&quot; Quashmallim. Part of the Occult Matrix that &quot;summons&quot; a new Angel is the G-M determining when a Quashmal will manifest. The other part being the G-M's own Angel Jacking - Hooking the Q's mind up to the Machine's data feeds, brainwashing them, reconfiguration to use the Essence supplied by Infrastructure instead of Pyros, and custom equipment/modifications to fulfill their designated purpose. It kind fits thematically, too: The Principle, and thus Quashmallim, care about choice - something the G-M, and thus its Angels, care not at all about (if not outright reject). This makes the <u>choice</u> of a Demon's Fall either the Principle in action, or an inherent bug in the design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit I love this.<br /> <br /> I'm playing in a Chronicle right now as a once-Exiled Angel that had made it her own purpose to find out what 'The Principle' is. She fell completely when she successfully drained Pyros from a Promethean, gaining an understanding of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> I never actually decided on what the Revelation she learned was.<br /> <br /> This is too perfect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:20:49-08:00","id":804699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804271-principle-renegades?p=804685#post804685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy shit I love this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your welcome. Honestly, I can't remember if someone said the same thing a year ago, or this was implicit subtext throughout the books. I just thought I'd mention it here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:20:33-08:00","id":804994,"title":"","content":"I think I like it better if GM angels are their own thing, but I really like the story potential here. <br /> <br /> The Cipher is all about growing, changing, and ultimately choice. The Cipher is a journey of self-discovery, and like a weary pilgrim the Unchained look to uncover their Final Truth. Perhaps the fallen ex-Exile will have a Final Truth that pushes them in the right direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}